; regression test for a bug found while adding `commit`: `break`/`commit` written at the very
; top level of a file (not inside any `sandbox` the file itself opened) used to crash with an
; internal `AssertionError` instead of a clean error -- a file's top level is *already* an
; implicit `sandbox` (see doc/kurt-doc.md's "Running a file itself already starts one level
; deep" note), so `break`/`commit` there used to happily close that hidden wrapper instead of
; refusing outright, breaking `load_file`'s own bookkeeping (it expects to be the only one
; popping that particular level). Fixed via `KnowledgeBase.is_load_boundary`, set only on that
; implicit level.
;
; note: this can't use `expect` (same reasoning as commit-only-closes-sandbox.kurt) -- the
; failure happens while `break`/`commit` itself tries to close a block, so the older `;;; `
; marker convention is used instead.
bool A
use A
break
;;; EvalError: `break` has no block to close here -- this is the top level of the file, not a `sandbox` you opened yourself
